# Every text file is LF in a checkout too, as .editorconfig asks. Fixtures, generated catalogs, style
# packs and starters are compared byte for byte (and by SHA-256) against what the app writes, and a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf turned them into CRLF: 24 unit tests and `icons:check` failed
# there, and the e2e gallery fixtures stopped matching their catalog. An existing Windows clone picks
# this up with `git checkout-index --force --all` once (commit or set aside local edits first).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The agent skill is compiled into the desktop app and installed byte for byte; its hash is pinned in
# src-tauri/src/agent/skill.rs. A Windows checkout must not turn its line endings into CRLF.
skills/** text eol=lf
